  "functional_objectives": [
    "THE CLI SHALL expose exactly the commands validate, summarize, explain, and schema and SHALL display all four command names in top-level help.",
    "THE CLI SHALL accept exactly these command forms: evidence-timeline validate INPUT [--format {text,json}] [--output OUTPUT_PATH]; evidence-timeline summarize INPUT [--format {text,json}] [--case-id CASE_ID] [--actor ACTOR] [--min-severity {debug,info,warning,error,critical}] [--tag TAG ...] [--redact] [--output OUTPUT_PATH]; evidence-timeline explain INPUT --event-id EVENT_ID [--format {text,json}] [--redact] [--output OUTPUT_PATH]; evidence-timeline schema [--format {text,json}] [--output OUTPUT_PATH].",
    "THE CLI SHALL require every command option to occur after its command, SHALL reject option abbreviation and aliases, SHALL reject every undeclared option, and SHALL interpret -- as the end of option parsing.",
    "THE CLI SHALL define --format with the exact values text and json and default text and SHALL define --output with default absent.",
    "THE CLI SHALL permit --case-id, --actor, --min-severity, and one or more --tag occurrences only on summarize and SHALL permit --redact only on summarize and explain.",
    "IF an invocation has a missing operand, extra operand, duplicate non-repeatable option, undeclared option, invalid --format value, invalid --min-severity value, unknown command, malformed option placement, or an option on a command that does not declare it, THEN THE CLI_Entrypoint SHALL emit exactly error: usage followed by one LF newline to stderr, emit nothing to stdout, read no input, and return exit code 2.",
    "IF --redact and --format json are supplied together, THEN THE CLI_Entrypoint SHALL emit exactly error: usage followed by one LF newline to stderr, emit nothing to stdout, read no input, and return exit code 2.",
    "THE CLI SHALL define one Event as an object having exactly the required keys event_id, case_id, timestamp, severity, actor, message, and tags and SHALL reject an object having a missing key or an additional key.",
    "THE CLI SHALL require event_id, case_id, actor, and message to be JSON strings containing at least one Unicode code point and SHALL NOT trim, normalize, case-fold, or otherwise rewrite those values.",
    "THE CLI SHALL require severity to be exactly one of the lowercase JSON strings debug, info, warning, error, and critical.",
    "THE CLI SHALL define severity rank as debug=0, info=1, warning=2, error=3, and critical=4.",
    "THE CLI SHALL require tags to be a JSON array of zero or more non-empty JSON strings and SHALL require every tag value to be unique by exact Unicode string equality within its Event.",
    "THE CLI SHALL allow no null value in an Event and SHALL treat a JSON boolean, number, object, array, or null in place of any declared string as an invalid Event.",
    "THE CLI SHALL require timestamp to be an RFC3339 timestamp of exactly YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ, YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS.fractionZ, YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS+HH:MM, YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS-HH:MM, YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS.fraction+HH:MM, or YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS.fraction-HH:MM, with uppercase T and Z, a fraction of one through six decimal digits when present, a real Gregorian date and time, second from 00 through 59, and an offset from -23:59 through +23:59.",
    "THE CLI SHALL reject a timestamp without an explicit Z or numeric offset and SHALL reject leap-second value 60.",
    "WHEN a valid timestamp is loaded, THE CLI SHALL convert it to UTC and represent Normalized_Timestamp as YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ when UTC microseconds equal zero and as YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS.ffffffZ with exactly six fractional digits otherwise.",
    "THE CLI SHALL require event_id to be unique by exact Unicode string equality across the complete input stream and SHALL treat every occurrence after the first occurrence of the same event_id as a duplicate-event-id record error.",
    "THE CLI SHALL define one JSONL record as one physical line decoded as UTF-8, excluding the line terminator, and SHALL treat an empty or whitespace-only physical line as a blank-line record error rather than skipping it.",
    "THE CLI SHALL accept CRLF or LF input line terminators and SHALL reject a file or stdin stream that cannot be decoded as UTF-8.",
    "THE CLI SHALL require each nonblank physical line to contain exactly one finite JSON object and SHALL reject invalid JSON, a non-object top-level JSON value, and the non-standard numeric constants NaN, Infinity, and -Infinity.",
    "THE CLI SHALL identify physical input lines by one-based LINE_NUMBER.",
    "THE CLI SHALL use exactly these record error codes: blank-line, invalid-json, invalid-event, and duplicate-event-id.",
    "WHEN validate reads the input, THE validate operation SHALL inspect every physical line in source order, SHALL retain no partial Event from an invalid line, and SHALL collect exactly one RecordError for each invalid physical line.",
    "THE CLI SHALL define RecordError as exactly {\"code\":RECORD_ERROR_CODE,\"line\":LINE_NUMBER} and SHALL order RecordError values by increasing LINE_NUMBER.",
    "WHEN validate finishes with no RecordError, THE validate operation SHALL return exactly ValidationPayload={\"errors\":[],\"records\":VALID_EVENT_COUNT,\"valid\":true} and return exit code 0.",
    "WHEN validate finishes with one or more RecordError values, THE validate operation SHALL return exactly ValidationPayload={\"errors\":[RecordError],\"records\":VALID_EVENT_COUNT,\"valid\":false}, emit no diagnostic to stderr, and return exit code 1 after the complete payload has been emitted or written.",
    "WHEN validate encounters a duplicate event_id, THE first structurally valid occurrence SHALL contribute to VALID_EVENT_COUNT and each later occurrence SHALL contribute one duplicate-event-id RecordError and SHALL NOT contribute to VALID_EVENT_COUNT.",
    "IF summarize or explain encounters the first invalid physical line in source order, THEN THE selected operation SHALL stop reading after that line, emit exactly error: invalid-jsonl:LINE_NUMBER:RECORD_ERROR_CODE followed by one LF newline to stderr, emit nothing to stdout, create or modify no output file, and return exit code 1.",
    "WHEN summarize or explain encounters a duplicate event_id, THE duplicate physical line rather than the first occurrence SHALL be the invalid line.",
    "THE CLI SHALL define EventView as exactly {\"actor\":ACTOR,\"case_id\":CASE_ID,\"event_id\":EVENT_ID,\"message\":MESSAGE,\"severity\":SEVERITY,\"tags\":[TAG],\"timestamp\":NORMALIZED_TIMESTAMP} with tags preserved in input order.",
    "THE CLI SHALL define Event_Order as ascending Normalized_Timestamp instant, then ascending exact Unicode case_id, then ascending exact Unicode event_id, without locale transformation, Unicode normalization, or case folding.",
    "WHEN summarize loads a valid input, THE summarize operation SHALL apply every supplied filter with logical AND before grouping and ordering events.",
    "WHERE --case-id CASE_ID is supplied, THE summarize operation SHALL retain only Events whose case_id exactly equals CASE_ID.",
    "WHERE --actor ACTOR is supplied, THE summarize operation SHALL retain only Events whose actor exactly equals ACTOR.",
    "WHERE --min-severity SEVERITY is supplied, THE summarize operation SHALL retain only Events whose severity rank is greater than or equal to the selected severity rank.",
    "WHERE one or more --tag TAG values are supplied, THE summarize operation SHALL retain only Events whose tags contain every supplied distinct TAG by exact Unicode string equality.",
    "THE CLI SHALL define CaseSummary as exactly {\"case_id\":CASE_ID,\"events\":[EventView],\"severity_counts\":{\"critical\":N,\"debug\":N,\"error\":N,\"info\":N,\"warning\":N}} with all five severity keys present, including zero counts.",
    "WHEN summarize succeeds, THE summarize operation SHALL return exactly SummaryPayload={\"cases\":[CaseSummary],\"event_count\":N}, SHALL order cases by ascending exact Unicode case_id, SHALL order each events array by Event_Order, and SHALL set N to the total number of retained Events.",
    "WHEN no Event remains after summarize filtering, THE summarize operation SHALL return exactly {\"cases\":[],\"event_count\":0} and return exit code 0.",
    "WHEN explain loads a valid input and exactly one Event has event_id equal to EVENT_ID, THE explain operation SHALL sort all Events of that Event's case by Event_Order and return the target Event, its immediate predecessor when one exists, and its immediate successor when one exists.",
    "THE CLI SHALL define ExplainPayload as exactly {\"case_id\":CASE_ID,\"events\":[EventView],\"target_event_id\":EVENT_ID}, SHALL order events by Event_Order, and SHALL include no Event from another case.",
    "WHEN the explained Event is the only Event in its case, THE explain operation SHALL include exactly the target Event in ExplainPayload.events.",
    "WHEN the explained Event is first or last in its case, THE explain operation SHALL include the target Event and only the one adjacent Event that exists.",
    "IF explain loads a valid input containing no Event whose event_id equals EVENT_ID, THEN THE explain operation SHALL emit exactly error: event-not-found followed by one LF newline to stderr, emit nothing to stdout, create or modify no output file, and return exit code 1.",
    "THE CLI SHALL resolve an event_id tie only through the duplicate-event-id invalid-input rule and SHALL NOT select one duplicate Event for explain.",
    "THE CLI SHALL define SchemaPayload as exactly {\"additional_fields\":false,\"fields\":{\"actor\":\"non-empty string\",\"case_id\":\"non-empty string\",\"event_id\":\"non-empty globally unique string\",\"message\":\"non-empty string\",\"severity\":\"debug|info|warning|error|critical\",\"tags\":\"array of unique non-empty strings\",\"timestamp\":\"RFC3339 timestamp with Z or numeric offset\"},\"nullable_fields\":[],\"required\":[\"event_id\",\"case_id\",\"timestamp\",\"severity\",\"actor\",\"message\",\"tags\"]}.",
    "WHEN schema is invoked, THE schema operation SHALL return exactly SchemaPayload, read no file or stdin, and return exit code 0.",
    "WHEN --format json is selected, THE CLI_Entrypoint SHALL serialize the applicable ValidationPayload, SummaryPayload, ExplainPayload, or SchemaPayload using Canonical_JSON and append exactly one LF newline.",
    "THE CLI SHALL define Canonical_JSON as UTF-8 JSON serialized with ensure_ascii=False, allow_nan=False, sort_keys=True, separators=(\",\",\":\"), and no serializer-owned trailing newline.",
    "WHEN validate --format text completes, THE CLI_Entrypoint SHALL emit exactly valid: true followed by LF and records: N followed by LF when valid, or valid: false followed by LF, records: N followed by LF, and one line line LINE_NUMBER: RECORD_ERROR_CODE for every RecordError in order when invalid.",
    "WHEN summarize --format text returns no Event, THE CLI_Entrypoint SHALL emit exactly No events. followed by one LF newline.",
    "WHEN summarize --format text returns Events, THE CLI_Entrypoint SHALL emit each case in case order as one header line case CASE_ID (N events), followed immediately by one line per Event in Event_Order formatted NORMALIZED_TIMESTAMP [SEVERITY] EVENT_ID actor=ACTOR tags=TAG_LIST MESSAGE, with TAG_LIST equal to - when tags is empty and otherwise the comma-joined tags in input order, and SHALL place no blank line between cases.",
    "WHEN explain --format text succeeds, THE CLI_Entrypoint SHALL emit the ExplainPayload Events in Event_Order using the summarize Event line format, prefixed by > and one space for the target Event and by two spaces for each context Event.",
    "WHEN schema --format text succeeds, THE CLI_Entrypoint SHALL emit exactly seven field lines in this order: event_id: non-empty globally unique string; case_id: non-empty string; timestamp: RFC3339 timestamp with Z or numeric offset; severity: debug|info|warning|error|critical; actor: non-empty string; message: non-empty string; tags: array of unique non-empty strings; with each field line terminated by LF.",
    "WHERE --redact is absent, THE CLI SHALL preserve every Event string exactly except timestamp normalization and format syntax.",
    "WHERE --redact is supplied with text format, THE CLI_Entrypoint SHALL apply redaction to case_id, event_id, actor, message, and every tag only after filtering, grouping, ordering, event lookup, and payload construction and before text rendering.",
    "THE CLI SHALL apply redaction replacements from left to right in this exact order: email, hexadecimal identifier, then long token.",
    "THE CLI SHALL define an email match through the Python regular expression (?i)(?<![A-Z0-9._%+-])[A-Z0-9._%+-]+@[A-Z0-9.-]+\\.[A-Z]{2,}(?![A-Z0-9.-]) and SHALL replace each non-overlapping match with [REDACTED_EMAIL].",
    "THE CLI SHALL define a hexadecimal identifier match through the Python regular expression (?i)(?<![0-9A-F])[0-9A-F]{16,}(?![0-9A-F]) and SHALL replace each non-overlapping match with [REDACTED_HEX].",
    "THE CLI SHALL define a long token match through the Python regular expression (?<![A-Za-z0-9_-])[A-Za-z0-9_-]{24,}(?![A-Za-z0-9_-]) and SHALL replace each non-overlapping match with [REDACTED_TOKEN].",
    "WHEN redaction changes a case_id used in a summarize text header, THE CLI_Entrypoint SHALL use the same redacted case_id in every Event line for that case.",
    "WHEN --output is absent, THE CLI_Entrypoint SHALL emit the declared result to stdout and SHALL create no output file.",
    "WHEN --output OUTPUT_PATH is supplied and the selected operation obtains a complete result, THE CLI_Entrypoint SHALL fully render and UTF-8 encode the result before opening or creating any output target, SHALL append exactly one LF newline as declared for stdout, SHALL write the identical result bytes to OUTPUT_PATH, and SHALL emit nothing to stdout or stderr.",
    "WHEN OUTPUT_PATH is relative, THE CLI_Entrypoint SHALL resolve it once against the invocation-start current working directory.",
    "WHEN a valid OUTPUT_PATH has missing parent directories, THE output operation SHALL create those parents only after input processing and result rendering have succeeded.",
    "IF OUTPUT_PATH identifies an existing directory, a symlink, or a path traversing an existing symlink ancestor, THEN THE CLI_Entrypoint SHALL emit exactly error: invalid-output-target followed by one LF newline to stderr, emit nothing to stdout, leave the target tree unchanged, and return exit code 1.",
    "IF OUTPUT_PATH identifies an existing regular non-symlink file, THEN the output operation SHALL atomically replace that file with the complete result bytes by writing a temporary sibling file and applying os.replace only after the temporary write succeeds.",
    "IF creating a parent, writing the temporary file, flushing, closing, or replacing OUTPUT_PATH fails, THEN THE CLI_Entrypoint SHALL emit exactly error: local-io followed by one LF newline to stderr, emit nothing to stdout, preserve an existing OUTPUT_PATH file unchanged when replacement has not completed, remove any temporary sibling created by the operation when possible, and return exit code 1.",
    "IF INPUT identifies a missing path, directory, unreadable file, symlink, or path traversing an existing symlink ancestor, or if INPUT cannot be decoded as UTF-8, THEN THE CLI_Entrypoint SHALL emit exactly error: local-io followed by one LF newline to stderr, emit nothing to stdout, create or modify no output file, and return exit code 1.",
    "THE CLI SHALL use exactly these public non-usage error forms: error: invalid-jsonl:LINE_NUMBER:RECORD_ERROR_CODE; error: event-not-found; error: invalid-output-target; and error: local-io.",
    "IF more than one non-usage expected failure is observable without performing a prohibited operation, THEN THE CLI SHALL select exactly one failure using this precedence: invalid-output-target; local-io for opening or decoding INPUT; invalid-jsonl; event-not-found; local-io for writing OUTPUT_PATH.",
    "WHEN the requirements phase identifies an input without one consumer, an option without one command matrix entry, a success without one exact logical payload, or a mutation without one declared target and failure policy, THE requirements workflow SHALL stop before design and request clarification.",
    "IF a public decision remains undefined, THEN THE requirements workflow SHALL NOT replace that decision with a placeholder, SHALL NOT defer it silently, and SHALL NOT generate design, tasks, or code."
